Modified work (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)): the OpenJevX model weights (openjevx.w8.onnx and the
fine-tune checkpoint) are not the original Laya or ModernBERT weights. They are fine-tuned from
convaiinnovations/laya (whose encoder is answerdotai/ModernBERT-large): encoder and decision head are
trained further on OpenJevX decision data, then calibrated and quantized to 8-bit by the OpenJevX project. Since model 0.5.8 the training
data is filtered to sources whose licence allows commercial use; the model archive lists what was left
out in licence-excluded.json.

